      "description": "Public webhook. Auth + resolution flow:\n\n1. RouterOS posts an `X-Router-Token` header (or `token` form field).\n2. The token is matched against `settings.webhook_token`.\n3. The router is resolved by `router_name`.\n4. The voucher sale is recorded idempotently by\n   `(router_id, username, sold_at)`.\n\nThe endpoint always returns 200 (even on validation/auth issues)\nso a misconfigured RouterOS scheduler does not loop on retries.\nOperators see issues via warnings in server logs.\n"
